Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 18:28:37 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 18/52] ci: run the latest VitaAutotests (#4227)

* ci: run the latest VitaAutotests

Move AUTOTESTS_REF to the VitaAutotests commit that adds 34 more tests,
and give each of them its outcome on Vita3K in expectations.txt. Five
of them pass, the others fail or crash on what each line says. The
names column is wider for the longer test names.

* kernel: refuse creating a lightweight mutex with no work area

Creating a lightweight mutex with a NULL work area wrote through the
NULL pointer, which crashes Vita3K on some hosts. It now fails with
ILLEGAL_ADDR, as on a Vita.

(cherry picked from commit 7e152b66e85345f175d3d287fcbd7f8abec7574a)
---
 vita3k/modules/SceKernelThreadMgr/SceThreadmgr.cpp | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/vita3k/modules/SceKernelThreadMgr/SceThreadmgr.cpp b/vita3k/modules/SceKernelThreadMgr/SceThreadmgr.cpp
index a275ac07..fb14cd61 100644
--- a/vita3k/modules/SceKernelThreadMgr/SceThreadmgr.cpp
+++ b/vita3k/modules/SceKernelThreadMgr/SceThreadmgr.cpp
@@ -57,6 +57,8 @@ static SceInt32 wait_event(EmuEnvState &emuenv, const char *export_name, SceUID
 
 EXPORT(int, __sceKernelCreateLwMutex, Ptr<SceKernelLwMutexWork> workarea, const char *name, unsigned int attr, Ptr<SceKernelCreateLwMutex_opt> opt) {
     TRACY_FUNC(__sceKernelCreateLwMutex, workarea, name, attr, opt);
+    if (!workarea)
+        return RET_ERROR(SCE_KERNEL_ERROR_ILLEGAL_ADDR);
     const int init_count = opt.get(emuenv.mem)->init_count;
     if (const SceInt32 error = Mutex::check_create(name, attr, init_count))
         return RET_ERROR(error);
